--- (1) THE EOS: FROM THE EQUILIBRIUM'S OWN RELATIONS (G084/G091/G031) ---
  inputs: the fixed baryon well Phi_b = C ln r, C = sqrt(G M_b a0) = v_flat^2
          [a0 enters ONLY as the observed asymptotic-RAR constant -- data, not a field]
  (i)   the equilibrium temperature:  sigma^2 = C/2 = 1.474730e+10 (m/s)^2;  sigma = 121.438 km/s
  (ii)  the isothermal EOS:            P = sigma^2 rho   (barotropic, G091 V1d)
  (iii) the phantom:                   rho = A/r^2, A = C/(4 pi G) = 3.516632e+19 kg/m
  THE HYDROSTATIC SELF-CONSTITENCY:    sigma^2 = 2 pi G A EXACTLY (rel err 0.00e+00)
        dP/dr = -rho GM(<r)/r^2 with M(<r) = 4 pi A r  =>  sigma^2 = 2 pi G A  [no field]
  THE CLOSED FORM:  P(rho) = (C/2) rho = (1/2) sqrt(G M_b a0) rho
        = 2 pi G A rho = G M_b rho/(2 r_M) = (a0 r_M/2) rho   -- one coefficient, four faces
        sigma^2 also = a0 r_M/2:  the a0 dependence is LINEAR in a0 (via r_M),
        sqrt(a0) through C:  rel err of the cross-forms = 1.29e-16
  THE a0-ONLY BOUNDARY VALUE (equipartition radius r = r_M):
        P(r_M) = a0^2/(8 pi G) = 5.2250e-12 Pa  [PURE a0, no M_b, no r]
        dimension check of the 'a0/G-class' guess: a0/G x rho = (kg/m^2)(kg/m^3)
        is NOT a pressure -- the correct a0-only pressure class is a0^2/G
  temperature from the equilibrium (NOT free): dS/dE at gamma = 2 = 1/sigma^2
        (G084 V1b: 6.780964e-11 vs 6.780902e-11 s^2/m^2; rel err 0.00%)
        T/m = sigma^2/k_B = 1.9041 mK per eV  (the EOS carries the equilibrium T)
  c_s^2 = dP/drho = C/2 = v_flat^2/2 (Q001);  w = P/(rho c^2) = (sigma/c)^2 = 1.641e-07

  the EOS along the equilibrium (both footings quoted once: canonical a0 = 9.3619e-11,
  alt 1.1279e-10 gives sigma = 124.9 km/s):
