    r_M (equipartition)      r =  10.2101 kpc   rho = 3.5430e-22 kg/m^3 (=    0.0052 Msun/pc^3)   P = 5.2250e-12 Pa   c_s = 121.44 km/s   w = 1.641e-07
    2 r_M (outside-cap)      r =  20.4201 kpc   rho = 8.8575e-23 kg/m^3 (=    0.0013 Msun/pc^3)   P = 1.3062e-12 Pa   c_s = 121.44 km/s   w = 1.641e-07

--- (2) ACROSS THE TRANSITION (G132's first-order boundary) ---
  the two-phase EOS:
    phantom branch (r <= r_break, rho >= rho_b):  P = sigma^2 rho = 1.3592e-11 Pa at the cap
    free-dust branch (r > r_break):               P ~ 0  (w = 0 EXACT, G031; collisionless, G103)
  THE JUMP at the cap:  dP = sigma^2 rho_b = 1.3592e-11 Pa
    a CONTACT DISCONTINUITY across a collisionless interface -- NOT a Maxwell
    equal-pressure construction: rho_ph/rho_d = A_b = 0.125-0.5 (G159 dressed,
    geomean 0.273), rho_d(cap) = 1.843e-21-7.374e-21 kg/m^3; the operative junction is the
    ENTROPY extremum (G159 V1; diffusive/chemical equilibrium blocked by 5 orders)
  the EOS's role AS the transition's thermodynamics:
    (a) the surface pressure at the cap IS the virial boundary term:
        3 P_s V = 1.2730e+51 J  vs  sigma^2 M_T = 1.2730e+51 J   [rel err 1.31e-16, G091 V1d re-verified]
    (b) the P-V work per particle across the boundary:
        w = P_b (m/rho_b) = m sigma^2 = k_B T_b = 1.3145e-22 J/particle   [EXACT, rel err 0.00e+00]
    (c) the latent heat (G132 committed): L/N = (dS/k_B) k_B T_b = 8.86 - 19.47 meV
    (d) THE IDENTITY TEST:  L/(N w) = dS/k_B = 10.80 - 23.73  !=  1
        the P-V work is NOT the latent heat: mechanical share w/(L/N) = 9.3% - 4.2%
        (water's P-V share of L at 373 K ~ 7%% -- SAME CLASS: the entropy step,
         not the mechanical work, dominates the first-order latent heat)
    reading: the EOS supplies the mechanical unit (k_B T_b per particle); G132's
            entropy bookkeeping supplies the latent heat; the two meet at dS/k_B.

